    "narrativeEn": "The first leg of the second qualifying round finished 1–1 at 3Arena on 23 July 2026.\n\nDino Studio · 23 July 2026 · Stockholm, Sweden\n\nHammarby and Anderlecht drew 1–1 at 3Arena in Stockholm on 23 July 2026 in the first leg of their UEFA Europa League second qualifying round tie. The result left the teams level ahead of the return meeting in Belgium.\n\nUEFA’s official draw paired the Swedish and Belgian clubs in the second round, with first legs scheduled for 23 July and return fixtures for 30 July. The governing body’s results and information kit confirm the 1–1 score in Stockholm.\n\nThe tie formed part of qualification for the 2026/27 Europa League. It was a two-leg contest, so the home result alone did not decide which club advanced. Anderlecht subsequently won the return 3–1 on 30 July, progressing 4–2 on aggregate.\n\nDino Studio’s photographs accompanying this report are from the opening match in Stockholm, identified in his original post by the date, stadium and score. They document the Swedish leg of the tie rather than the later return fixture in Brussels.",
