    "narrativeEn": "A 3–1 victory at 3Arena restores Hammarby’s momentum.\n\nDino Studio · 13 September 2026 · 3Arena, Stockholm, Sweden\n\nHammarby beat Brommapojkarna 3–1 at 3Arena on 13 September 2026 in the 21st round of Allsvenskan. The home side returned to winning ways after a derby defeat against AIK and a draw away to Örgryte.\n\nPaulos Abraham put Hammarby ahead in the eighth minute, finishing a low free-kick delivery from Victor Lind. Brommapojkarna defended compactly before beginning to establish possession higher up the pitch. Their equaliser arrived when Oliver Zandén reached the left byline and found Mads Hansen, who finished with one touch.\n\nHammarby recovered the lead in first-half stoppage time through Markus Karlsson. A third goal early in the second half, with Lind again providing the decisive delivery, gave the hosts a firmer grip on the contest. Official Allsvenskan Fantasy records identify Frederik Winther as the scorer.\n\nBrommapojkarna introduced attacking substitutes but could not find a route back into the game. The visitors’ club report recorded an attendance of 25,252 and described a match in which Hammarby’s sustained pressure ultimately proved decisive.",
    "narrativeSv": "En 3–1-seger på 3Arena gav Hammarby förnyad energi i Allsvenskan.\n\nDino Studio · 13 september 2026 · 3Arena, Stockholm, Sverige\n\nHammarby besegrade Brommapojkarna med 3–1 på 3Arena den 13 september 2026 i Allsvenskans 21:a omgång. Hemmalaget återvände till vinnarspåret efter en derbyförlust och ett oavgjort resultat borta mot Örgryte.\n\nPaulos Abraham gav Hammarby ledningen i den åttonde minuten på frispark från Victor Lind. Brommapojkarna kvitterade genom Mads Hansen innan Markus Karlsson återtog ledningen på stopptid i första halvlek. Frederik Winther fastställde slutresultatet i andra halvlek inför 25 252 åskådare. Dino Studios bilder fångar matchsekvenserna och målfirandet.",
