    "narrativeEn": "Hammarby beat IFK Kristianstad 31–26 after building a six-goal first-half lead.\n\nDino Studio · 28 March 2025 · Eriksdalshallen, Stockholm\n\nHammarby defeated IFK Kristianstad 31–26 at Eriksdalshallen on 28 March 2025, taking a 2–0 lead in their Handbollsligan quarter-final series. An assertive first half established the platform for a second consecutive play-off victory.\n\nHammarby opened an 8–1 advantage as Kristianstad struggled to find a way through the home defence. Goalkeeper Linus Bergh made several early saves, while Oliver Wigmark contributed on the counterattack. Hammarby reached half-time with a 19–13 lead.\n\nKristianstad responded with four consecutive goals after the break, closing to 19–17 before Hammarby regained momentum. The home side later stretched the margin to 26–20 and held off another response in the closing minutes.\n\nWigmark finished as Hammarby’s leading scorer with nine goals, including two penalties. Josef Pujol added four, while five teammates scored three each. The club recorded an attendance of 1,718. The victory gave Hammarby the opportunity to decide the series in the next meeting in Kristianstad. Dino Studio’s photographs document the Stockholm quarter-final.",
    "narrativeSv": "Hammarby besegrade IFK Kristianstad med 31–26 efter ett sexmålsöverläge i paus.\n\nDino Studio · 28 mars 2025 · Eriksdalshallen, Stockholm\n\nHammarby besegrade IFK Kristianstad med 31–26 i Eriksdalshallen den 28 mars 2025 och tog därmed en 2–0-ledning i kvartsfinalserien i Handbollsligan. En stark första halvlek lade grunden för hemmasegern inför 1 718 åskådare.\n\nHammarby ryckte åt sig en 8–1-ledning tidigt då Kristianstad hade svårt att ta sig förbi hemmaförsvaret och målvakten Linus Bergh. Oliver Wigmark blev bäste målskytt med nio mål. Dino Studios bilder dokumenterar kvartsfinaldramatiken i Eriksdalshallen.",
