    "narrativeEn": "Rehnberg and Hasund secure a 2–0 Damallsvenskan victory.\n\nDino Studio · 5 September 2026 · Hammarby IP, Stockholm, Sweden\n\nHammarby defeated IFK Norrköping 2–0 at Hammarby IP on 5 September 2026, scoring both goals after a goalless first half in the 17th round of OBOS Damallsvenskan.\n\nNorrköping remained compact before the interval and created an early opportunity when Malva Larsson met a corner, only to direct her header into goalkeeper Cajsa Andersson’s arms. The visitors’ defensive organisation kept the contest level at the break.\n\nFormer Norrköping player Svea Rehnberg opened the scoring for Hammarby with a header in the 52nd minute. Norrköping looked for a response, with substitute Emma Engström attempting to reach Carrie Jones’s delivery across the penalty area.\n\nThe visitors’ push forward also opened space for Hammarby, and Vilde Hasund added the second goal in the 72nd minute. Engström later had another opportunity but shot wide, leaving Norrköping without a goal.\n\nThe away club’s match report recorded a crowd of 1,343. Hammarby finished with three points and a clean sheet, while Norrköping were left to reflect on chances they could not convert.",
    "narrativeSv": "Rehnberg och Hasund säkrade en 2–0-seger i Damallsvenskan.\n\nDino Studio · 5 september 2026 · Hammarby IP, Stockholm, Sverige\n\nHammarby besegrade IFK Norrköping med 2–0 på Hammarby IP den 5 september 2026, efter två mål i den andra halvleken i OBOS Damallsvenskans 17:e omgång.\n\nSvea Rehnberg nickade in ledningsmålet i den 52:a minuten och Vilde Hasund fastställde slutresultatet i den 72:a minuten inför 1 343 åskådare. Hammarby säkrade tre poäng och höll nollan. Dino Studios fotografier dokumenterar seriematchen på Södermalm.",
