    "narrativeEn": "Sweden’s final pre-tournament home match ends 2–2.\n\nDino Studio · 4 June 2026 · Strawberry Arena, Solna, Sweden\n\nSweden drew 2–2 with Greece at Strawberry Arena on 4 June 2026 in their final match before departing for the World Cup in North America. A late equaliser denied the hosts victory after they had overturned a first-half deficit.\n\nKostas Tsimikas gave Greece the lead in the tenth minute, finishing from inside the Swedish penalty area. Greece maintained that advantage until the interval.\n\nViktor Gyökeres brought Sweden level with a free-kick in the 53rd minute, registering his 20th senior international goal. Following extensive substitutions, Sweden moved in front in the 69th minute. Taha Ali beat the Greek defence on the left and delivered the ball for Gustaf Nilsson to finish from close range.\n\nGreece responded deep into added time. Giorgos Masouras met a delivery from Charalampos Kostoulas to score in the fifth minute of stoppage time and settle the result.\n\nThe draw concluded Sweden’s home preparations. The Swedish Football Association confirmed that the squad’s next step was departure for North America, with Dallas serving as its tournament base.",
    "narrativeSv": "Sveriges sista hemmalandskamp inför mästerskapet slutade 2–2 efter en sen grekisk kvittering.\n\nDino Studio · 4 juni 2026 · Strawberry Arena, Solna, Sverige\n\nSverige spelade 2–2 mot Grekland på Strawberry Arena den 4 juni 2026 i sin sista match före avresan till VM i Nordamerika. En sen kvittering från gästerna berövade Sverige segern efter en händelserik landskamp i Solna. Dino Studios fotografier dokumenterar landslagets VM-genrep.",
