    "narrativeEn": "Sweden recovered from an early setback to beat Italy in the Women’s Nations League at Strawberry Arena.\n\nDino Studio · 4 April 2025 · Solna, Sweden\n\nSweden defeated Italy 3–2 at Strawberry Arena on 4 April 2025, with Fridolina Rolfö converting the decisive penalty in the fourth minute of second-half stoppage time. The Women’s Nations League match brought two changes of momentum before the home side secured the victory.\n\nItaly struck almost immediately. Emma Severini finished a move involving Chiara Beccari in the opening minute, leaving Sweden to chase the game. The home side eventually equalised through captain Kosovare Asllani in the 56th minute. Filippa Angeldahl then put Sweden ahead with a free kick in the 75th.\n\nMichela Cambiaghi restored parity for Italy in the 85th minute, setting up a tense finish. Rolfö’s late penalty settled the contest and completed Sweden’s comeback.\n\nThe result came in League A of the Nations League. Sweden’s next scheduled match was against Wales at Gamla Ullevi. Dino Studio’s photographs from the Sweden–Italy match accompany this report from the national arena in Solna.",
    "narrativeSv": "Sverige vände underläge och besegrade Italien i Women’s Nations League på Strawberry Arena efter Rolfös straff på tilläggstid.\n\nDino Studio · 4 april 2025 · Solna, Sverige\n\nSverige besegrade Italien med 3–2 på Strawberry Arena den 4 april 2025 där Fridolina Rolfö satte den avgörande straffen på stopptid i Women’s Nations League. Dino Studios bilder dokumenterar matchhändelserna och det dramatiska avgörandet i Solna.",
