    "summaryEn": "Thorengruppen defeated FBC Kalmarsund 4–2 in the women’s Swedish championship final. (20 match photographs).",
    "summarySv": "Thorengruppen besegrade FBC Kalmarsund med 4–2 i damernas SM-final i innebandy. (20 matchbilder).",
    "narrativeEn": "Thorengruppen defeated FBC Kalmarsund 4–2 in the women’s Swedish championship final.\n\nDino Studio · 25 April 2026 · Avicii Arena, Stockholm\n\nThorengruppen IBK defeated FBC Kalmarsund 4–2 at Avicii Arena on 25 April 2026 to secure a sixth consecutive Swedish women’s floorball championship. Two goals in the third period decided a final that had remained level through its first two periods.\n\nA crowd of 10,116 watched the teams contest the title in Stockholm, according to Svensk Innebandy’s official report. The match reached the first interval at 2–2, and a scoreless second period left the outcome unresolved heading into the last twenty minutes.\n\nKalmarsund created several clear chances, but Thorengruppen made their opportunities count when the deciding moments arrived. Their late breakthrough extended the club’s championship run and denied Kalmarsund the title.\n\nThe final also marked the end of Emelie Wibron’s playing career. The federation’s regional annual report credits her with a hat-trick in her farewell appearance. Dino Studio’s photographs document the women’s final and the closing stage of the Swedish championship season in Avicii Arena.",
    "narrativeSv": "Thorengruppen besegrade FBC Kalmarsund med 4–2 i damernas SM-final i innebandy.\n\nDino Studio · 25 april 2026 · Avicii Arena, Stockholm\n\nThorengruppen IBK besegrade FBC Kalmarsund med 4–2 i Avicii Arena den 25 april 2026 och bärgade sitt sjätte raka SM-guld i innebandy för damer. Två mål i tredje perioden avgjorde en final som stått 2–2 efter två perioder inför 10 116 åskådare. Dino Studios fotografier dokumenterar SM-finalen och guldceremonin i Avicii Arena.",
